	  ====================================
			SPECIAL QUALITIES
	  ====================================
	  ====================================-->
	<special_qualities>
		<!-- Visible All "Special Ability" Ability Objects -->
		<special_quality>
			<name>Elven Immunities</name>
			<description>Elves are immune to magic sleep effects and get a +2 racial saving throw bonus against enchantment spells and effects.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.ELF RACIAL TRAIT.ELF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>SaveBonus: +2 racial saving throw bonus against enchantment spells and effects.</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.20</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Elven Magic</name>
			<description>Elves receive a +2 racial bonus on caster level checks made to overcome spell resistance. In addition, elves receive a +2 racial bonus on Spellcraft skill checks made to identify the properties of magic items.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.ELF RACIAL TRAIT.ELF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY.SPECIAL QUALITY.ELVEN MAGIC</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.20</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Evasion (Ex)</name>
			<description>You can avoid damage from many area-effect attacks. If you make a successful Reflex saving throw against an attack that normally deals half damage on a successful save, you instead take no damage. Evasion can only be used if you are wearing light armor or no armor. If you are helpless, you do not gain the benefit of evasion.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.DEFENSIVE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Immunity to Sleep (Ex)</name>
			<description>You are never subject to sleep effects.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.IMMUNITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Immunity: Sleep</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Bestiary, p.301</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Keen Senses</name>
			<description>Elves receive a +2 racial bonus on Perception skill checks.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.ELF RACIAL TRAIT.ELF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.20</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Low-Light Vision (Ex)</name>
			<description>Elves can see twice as far as humans in conditions of dim light.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.ELF RACIAL TRAIT.ELF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.RACIAL VISION</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.20</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Trapfinding (Ex)</name>
			<description>You add +2 to Perception skill checks made to locate traps and to Disable Device skill checks. You can use the Disable Device skill to disarm magical traps.</description>
			<type>ROGUECLASSFEATURES.RANGERCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.TRAPFINDING</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook, p.68</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Trap Sense (Ex)</name>
			<description>You gain a +1 bonus on Reflex saves made to avoid traps, and a +1 dodge bonus to AC against attacks made by traps.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.DEFENSIVE.BARBARIANCLASSFEATURES.CLASSFEATURES</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Ability Benefit: +1, SaveBonus: +1 Reflex to avoid traps</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Uncanny Dodge (Ex)</name>
			<description>You can react to danger before your senses would normally allow you to do so. You cannot be caught flat-footed, nor do you lose your Dexterity bonus to AC if the attacker is invisible. You still lose your Dexterity bonus to AC if immobilized. You can still lose your Dexterity bonus to AC if an opponent successfully uses the feint action against you.</description>
			<type>SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.DEFENSIVE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Weapon Familiarity</name>
			<description>Elves are proficient with longbows (including composite longbows), longswords, rapiers, and shortbows (including composite shortbows), and treat any weapon with the word &quot;elven&quot; in its name as a martial weapon.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.ELF RACIAL TRAIT.ELF RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY.SPECIAL QUALITY.WEAPON FAMILIARITY.RACIALWEAPONFAMILIARITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.20</source>
		</special_quality>
	</special_qualities>
	<!--
	  ====================================
	  ====================================
			SPECIAL ATTACKS
	  ====================================
	  ====================================-->
	<special_attacks>
		<!-- Visible All "Special Ability" Ability Objects -->
		<special_attack>
			<name>Assault Leader (Ex)</name>
			<description>Once per day, when the rogue misses with an attack on a flanked opponent, she can designate a single ally who is also flanking the target that her attack missed. That ally can make a single melee attack against the opponent as an immediate action.</description>
			<type>ROGUETALENT.SPECIALATTACK.EXTRAORDINARY.ATTACKOPTION.UNCHAINED ROGUE TALENT</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>CheckCount: 1, CheckType: Uses per Day</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Player&#39;s Guide, p.130</source>
		</special_attack>
		<special_attack>
			<name>Befuddling Strike (Ex)</name>
			<description>When the rogue deals sneak attack damage against an opponent, that opponent takes a -2 penalty on attack rolls against the rogue for 1d4 rounds.</description>
			<type>ROGUETALENT.SPECIALATTACK.EXTRAORDINARY.ATTACKOPTION.POISONDARTERTALENTCHOICE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Player&#39;s Guide, p.130</source>
		</special_attack>
		<special_attack>
			<name>Sneak Attack (Ex)</name>
			<description>If you can catch an opponent when he is unable to defend himself effectively from your attack, you can strike a vital spot for extra damage. Your attack deals 2d6 points of extra damage anytime your target would be denied a Dexterity bonus to AC, or when you flank your target. Should you score a critical hit with a sneak attack, this extra damage is not multiplied. Ranged attacks can count as sneak attacks only if the target is within 30 feet. With a weapon that deals nonlethal damage, you can make a sneak attack that deals nonlethal damage instead of lethal damage. You cannot use a weapon that deals lethal damage to deal nonlethal damage in a sneak attack, not even with the usual -4 penalty. You must be able to see the target well enough to pick out a vital spot and must be able to reach such a spot. You cannot sneak attack while striking a creature with concealment.</description>
			<type>ROGUECLASSFEATURES.ALCHEMISTCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALATTACK.EXTRAORDINARY.ATTACKOPTION.UNCHAINED ROGUE CLASS FEATURE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Ability Benefit: 2d6</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook, p.68</source>
		</special_attack>
	</special_attacks>

